 "build": {
  "id": "06a3a629-dd8e-4c6f-a0e1-6e9e17d63f74",
  "title": "Wildwalker AoE Dungeon Build",
  "description": "[overview]\nThis is an AoE-focused build with decent single-target for bosses with CDs. I've only been playing Primalist since the project started and have tried min-maxing different builds for each melee spec.\n\n[talents]\nKey talents here are Pulverize, Elemental Berserker, Totemic Echoes, Torn to Shreds, Spiritual Frenzy, Wild Carnage, and Totem Warrior.\n\nFlex talents can be Wild At Heart; this talent is only good if you can keep your rage up to spam Wildclaws fast enough. If you need more single-target damage for raids, remove Wild Carnage with Rylak's Blessing.\n\n[rotation]\nKey Rotation:\n\nOpen with Grove Guardian>Totemic Smash> Primal Shred>Boulder Dash>Seismic Spike. Then spam Wildclaws until Totemic Smash is off CD.\n \nMaintain Primal Shred and Torn to Shreds on all targets for rage/procs, and keep Wild Carnage buffed up every 6s by using Seismic Spike.\n\nST: Same opener, but instead of Seismic Spike, use Seismic Crash unless you need to cleave. Pop Primal Convergence and Savage Frenzy to increase DPS. \n\n*Grove Guardians is uncapped aoe dps and should always be taken.\n\n[stats]\nAttack Power and Strength will be your top stats. \n\nCrit will be your best secondary stat since we use Wildclaws as a substitute for attack speed.\n\nBe sure to get hit capped and some expertise.*\n\n\n\n\n* Still working on bis gear list and stats.\n\n[tips]\nI highly recommend running your pet on passive and macro /petattack into your key ST abilities.\n\nBIS Pet: Wolf; it has a 20s AOE attack power buff on a 40s CD and an additional 20s 10% attack power buff on a 5-minute CD.",
  "class_id": 31,
  "spec_id": 82,
